[1.3383, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.3802, "o", "VACUOUS COMPLETENESS THEOREMS\r\n\r\n  models in the file            250\r\n  with `functions := []`        114\r\n  ...and an empty Env too       104\r\n  counted by max_vacuous        44\r\n  vacuous and INVISIBLE to it   70\r\n\r\n`max_vacuous` counts only models that ALSO disagree with the Rust classifier.\r\nA theorem about an empty module says nothing about its spec whether or not the\r\nclassifier happens to disagree, so the ratchet measures a subset of its own\r\nsubject -- and the number it reports looks like the number you care about.\r\n\r\nRead from the file's text. Only a Lean build can say what these theorems MEAN,\r\nand no workflow in this repository builds them (#2747).\r\n"]
